Hand-written, not the generic "autotools" template the manifest.tsv row
still names (manifest build-type field is stale/unused for this port -
do not resync from it). CMake has its own bootstrap script producing a
plain Makefile, not a normal autotools ./configure - see the comment in
build() for -DCMAKE_USE_OPENSSL=OFF, which is the load-bearing fix
(prevents CMake's vendored librhash from linking a stray libcrypto.so.3
instead of Arctic's LibreSSL libcrypto.so.57).
